{"name":"Window Grey","hex":"#989ea1","fetched":"2026-10-13","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"window","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["An opening, usually covered by one or more panes of clear glass, to allow light and air from outside to enter a building or vehicle.","An opening, usually covered by glass, in a shop which allows people to view the shop and its products from outside; a shop window."]},{"part":"Verb","definitions":["To furnish with windows.","To place at or in a window."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/window"},{"term":"grey","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Adjective","definitions":["Commonwealth standard spelling of gray.","Synonym of coloured (pertaining to the mixed race of black and white)."]},{"part":"Verb","definitions":["Commonwealth standard spelling of gray."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/grey"}],"entries":[{"title":"Window","blocks":[{"text":"A window is an opening in a wall, door, roof, or vehicle that allows the exchange of light and sometimes allows the passage of sound and air. Modern windows are usually glazed, or covered in some other transparent or translucent material, a sash set in a frame in the opening. The sash and frame are also referred to as a window. Many glazed windows may be opened, to allow ventilation, or closed to exclude inclement weather. Windows may have a latch or similar mechanism to lock the window shut or to hold it open by various amounts."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/6/64/Atua_Kosua_shrine4.jpg/330px-Atua_Kosua_shrine4.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Window","wikidata":"Q35473"},{"title":"Grey","blocks":[{"text":"Grey or gray is an intermediate color between black and white. It is a neutral or achromatic color, meaning that it has no chroma. It is the color of a rain or storm cloud, of ash, and of lead."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commo